research/audit/wave11-certifier-tasks/ex-two-root-x-and-its-unbounded-derivative.md:396:  "rationale": "The CLP university text computes (sqrt x)'=1/(2sqrt x) for x>0 and states that the derivative is undefined at zero; Active Calculus treats 1/sqrt x as an unbounded integrand at zero. The item scales by 2, proves the precise unbounded sequence, and packages those facts to explain why the proper Riemann FTC does not apply on [0,1].",
