research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.findings.md:127:The A-page summary `library/real-analysis/properties-of-the-integral-and-the-working-ftc.md` says Taylor's integral remainder “is deliberately developed” on the Darboux/l'Hopital/Taylor page. The published target's scope remark says exactly the opposite: “No integral remainder ... is made here.” `rem-integral-conventions-and-scope` accurately describes only the old scaffold plan and also says the result is absent from the integral page. This is stale page-plan prose, not a false mathematical theorem; it is recorded for the publication-maintenance queue under the triage rule and was not chased or edited.
