research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1009657-+{"id":"cex-a-composition-of-integrable-functions-that-is-not-integrable","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00591-022-00318-x"],"rationale":"The peer-reviewed source gives the same counterexample: Thomae's Riemann-integrable function composed with the integrable indicator of the positive range becomes Dirichlet's nonintegrable function. The repository's discontinuity-set verification is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
