research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1023857-+{"id":"fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"The fat-Cantor compression construction is recognizably part of established real-analysis counterexample practice, but no semantically identical reputable source surfaced after searches for the precise Riemann-substitution failure. The on-disk proof was checked through continuity of distance, strict increase of its integral, nullity of the image, and the Lebesgue criterion. Under the hard non-invention default this remains established-knowledge pending Alpha concurrence.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
