research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1052448-+{"id":"ex-additivity-on-a-step-function","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"The particular two-level step function and its paired verification routes are a local worked construction. Splitting at 1 gives two constant integrals 1 and 3, and the displayed three-point Darboux partition gives matching sums after the single jump is isolated; the value 4 is directly verified.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1052449-+{"id":"ex-integral-test-applied-to-the-p-series","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_series.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_impropriemann.html"],"rationale":"The sources give the p-series threshold p>1 and the integral test. The item specializes to rational powers available in the library, indexes f_p(t)=(t+1)^{-p} from zero, and expresses improper convergence as boundedness of its proper-integral sequence. The mathematical threshold is sourced, but its last p=1 sentence falsely denies existence of a primitive and is proposed for repair.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:1052450:+{"id":"ex-two-root-x-and-its-unbounded-derivative","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www2.hawaii.edu/~gradysw/apex/sec_derivative.html","https://faculty.gvsu.edu/boelkinm/Home/ACS/sec-6-5-improper.html"],"rationale":"The sources state that sqrt(x) is continuous, has derivative 1/(2sqrt(x)) for x>0, is not differentiable at zero, and has an unbounded derivative near zero. The item scales by 2 and packages those facts to explain why the proper Riemann FTC does not apply on [0,1].","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1052451-+{"id":"cex-an-integrable-function-with-no-primitive","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html","https://math.colgate.edu/math323/dlantz/extras/notesC5.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the sign function's integral function as an absolute-value function and Darboux's theorem that derivatives cannot jump. The item packages these standard facts as an explicit refutation of the claim that every Riemann-integrable function has a primitive.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1052452-+{"id":"cex-a-function-with-a-primitive-that-is-not-integrable","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"none","urls":[],"rationale":"The exact disjoint-interval quartic bump construction is a bespoke polynomial replacement for the classical trigonometric witness. The proof checks seam derivatives, differentiability at the accumulation point, and the displayed unbounded derivative values directly. No semantically identical source for this construction surfaced, and its deliberate coefficient and interval design supports the positive local-invention determination.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1052453-+{"id":"cex-a-composition-of-integrable-functions-that-is-not-integrable","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00591-022-00318-x"],"rationale":"The peer-reviewed source gives the same counterexample: Thomae's Riemann-integrable function composed with the integrable indicator of the positive range becomes Dirichlet's nonintegrable function. The repository's discontinuity-set verification is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
--
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1052456-+{"id":"cex-the-first-mean-value-theorem-needs-a-one-signed-weight","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"The locally selected witness f(t)=g(t)=t on [-1,1] directly refutes deletion of the one-sign hypothesis: integral g is zero while integral fg=integral t^2=2/3 is positive. Every computation follows immediately from the already cited polynomial integral and symmetry facts.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1052457-+{"id":"fs-integration-by-parts-needs-no-integrability-hypothesis","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"none","urls":[],"rationale":"This exact undefinedness refutation is a bespoke composition of the preceding local quartic-bump function G with v(x)=x. The proof directly verifies that G is integrable while xG' remains unbounded at the displayed bump points, so one integral in the asserted equation does not denote.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1052458-+{"id":"fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"The fat-Cantor compression construction is recognizably part of established real-analysis counterexample practice, but no semantically identical reputable source surfaced after searches for the precise Riemann-substitution failure. The on-disk proof was checked through continuity of distance, strict increase of its integral, nullity of the image, and the Lebesgue criterion. Under the hard non-invention default this remains established-knowledge pending Alpha concurrence.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:1052459:+{"id":"fs-the-integral-function-is-always-a-primitive","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html"],"rationale":"The source states the precise FTC continuity-point condition and gives the sign-function integral whose absolute-value cusp is not differentiable. The item combines that canonical witness with the standard finite-point-change witness to distinguish nonexistence of F' from existence with F' not equal to f.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
