research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1119589-+{"id":"cex-a-function-with-a-primitive-that-is-not-integrable","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"none","urls":[],"rationale":"The exact disjoint-interval quartic bump construction is a bespoke polynomial replacement for the classical trigonometric witness. The proof checks seam derivatives, differentiability at the accumulation point, and the displayed unbounded derivative values directly. No semantically identical source for this construction surfaced, and its deliberate coefficient and interval design supports the positive local-invention determination.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1119590-+{"id":"cex-a-composition-of-integrable-functions-that-is-not-integrable","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00591-022-00318-x"],"rationale":"The peer-reviewed source gives the same counterexample: Thomae's Riemann-integrable function composed with the integrable indicator of the positive range becomes Dirichlet's nonintegrable function. The repository's discontinuity-set verification is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
--
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1119593-+{"id":"cex-the-first-mean-value-theorem-needs-a-one-signed-weight","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"The locally selected witness f(t)=g(t)=t on [-1,1] directly refutes deletion of the one-sign hypothesis: integral g is zero while integral fg=integral t^2=2/3 is positive. Every computation follows immediately from the already cited polynomial integral and symmetry facts.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1119594-+{"id":"fs-integration-by-parts-needs-no-integrability-hypothesis","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"none","urls":[],"rationale":"This exact undefinedness refutation is a bespoke composition of the preceding local quartic-bump function G with v(x)=x. The proof directly verifies that G is integrable while xG' remains unbounded at the displayed bump points, so one integral in the asserted equation does not denote.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1119595-+{"id":"fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"The fat-Cantor compression construction is recognizably part of established real-analysis counterexample practice, but no semantically identical reputable source surfaced after searches for the precise Riemann-substitution failure. The on-disk proof was checked through continuity of distance, strict increase of its integral, nullity of the image, and the Lebesgue criterion. Under the hard non-invention default this remains established-knowledge pending Alpha concurrence.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:1119596:+{"id":"fs-the-integral-function-is-always-a-primitive","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html"],"rationale":"The source states the precise FTC continuity-point condition and gives the sign-function integral whose absolute-value cusp is not differentiable. The item combines that canonical witness with the standard finite-point-change witness to distinguish nonexistence of F' from existence with F' not equal to f.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
