research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1176569-+{"id":"cex-the-first-mean-value-theorem-needs-a-one-signed-weight","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"The locally selected witness f(t)=g(t)=t on [-1,1] directly refutes deletion of the one-sign hypothesis: integral g is zero while integral fg=integral t^2=2/3 is positive. Every computation follows immediately from the already cited polynomial integral and symmetry facts.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1176570-+{"id":"fs-integration-by-parts-needs-no-integrability-hypothesis","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"none","urls":[],"rationale":"This exact undefinedness refutation is a bespoke composition of the preceding local quartic-bump function G with v(x)=x. The proof directly verifies that G is integrable while xG' remains unbounded at the displayed bump points, so one integral in the asserted equation does not denote.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1176571-+{"id":"fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"The fat-Cantor compression construction is recognizably part of established real-analysis counterexample practice, but no semantically identical reputable source surfaced after searches for the precise Riemann-substitution failure. The on-disk proof was checked through continuity of distance, strict increase of its integral, nullity of the image, and the Lebesgue criterion. Under the hard non-invention default this remains established-knowledge pending Alpha concurrence.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:1176572:+{"id":"fs-the-integral-function-is-always-a-primitive","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html"],"rationale":"The source states the precise FTC continuity-point condition and gives the sign-function integral whose absolute-value cusp is not differentiable. The item combines that canonical witness with the standard finite-point-change witness to distinguish nonexistence of F' from existence with F' not equal to f.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
