research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1205106-+{"id":"def-the-integral-function","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Integral_calculus","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html"],"rationale":"The sources define the variable-upper-limit integral function F(x)=integral_a^x f. The item merely fixes the same object in the library's oriented-integral notation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
