research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1419761-+{"id":"cex-an-integrable-function-with-no-primitive","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html","https://math.colgate.edu/math323/dlantz/extras/notesC5.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the sign function's integral function as an absolute-value function and Darboux's theorem that derivatives cannot jump. The item packages these standard facts as an explicit refutation of the claim that every Riemann-integrable function has a primitive.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
